# From "Remote Viewing" (Wave III - Freedom, CD1-2). Stays at F10 throughout
# -- the tape never climbs to F12. Reaches for energy-bar-tool.gws by name and
# reshapes it into a tube for perception, then back into a bar for the
# telekinesis-style practice on a visualised cotton ball, then a tube again
# for contacting someone known. Three distinct applications of the same tool,
# kept together because the tape bundles them as one exercise.

@segment   remote-viewing
@title     Remote Viewing
@levels    F10
@duration  ~6m
@protected Energy Bar Tool

say Reach out and find your Energy Bar Tool. Bring it close, and charge it with fresh energy.
pause 6
say Now reshape it. Change the bar into a tube of energy — you made it, so you can remake it.
pause 8
say Place one end close to your center of consciousness. Stretch the other end out, as far as you like, until it reaches the sealed envelope you're picturing — the one with a card inside, six numbers written on it.
pause 10
say Perceive through the tube. Read the six numbers, one at a time. You'll remember them clearly once you're back awake.
pause 15
say Now pull the tube back. Let it shrink to its normal size, and charge it again with bright white energy.
pause 8
say Change your tool back into a solid bar. Picture a white cotton ball in front of you.
pause 6
say Press the charged bar against it, and let energy flow out — making the ball lighter, and lighter, until it starts to float upward on its own.
pause 10
say Now cut the energy. Let the ball fall back down, and recharge your bar.
pause 8
say Try it again — touch the ball, send lifting energy, and let it float. Then cut the energy and recharge.
pause 10
say Now something different. Touch the ball again, and this time send heating energy — warmer, and warmer, until it's hot enough to smoke. Then cut the energy completely, and pull your tool back to recharge. Nothing more flows to the ball.
pause 12
say Reshape your tool into a tube once more. One end close to your center of consciousness — stretch the other end out to someone you know, wherever they are right now.
pause 8
say Perceive through the tube. What are they doing? Where are they? What are they thinking? Let it flow to you, and remember it clearly.
pause 15
say Now, if you wish, send a message through the same tube — clear and strong — to let them know you're here.
pause 10
say Pull the tube back to its normal size, and change it back into a bar. Put it away somewhere you can find it again.
pause 8
